+Use case: compositing. Photorealistic website hero image EDIT, wide 8:5 landscape.
+INPUTS: Image 1 (refs/background.png) is the EDIT TARGET and original sky / navigation background. Image 2 (v2/branch-01.png) is scale, realism, generous foliage, and composition reference ONLY. Images 3–5 (refs/7.png, refs/8.png, refs/9.png) are botanical texture references only; do not copy any reference watermark or checkerboard.
+
+Add ONE abandoned futuristic machine sculpture shaped like an enormous irregular tree limb, reclaimed by decades of vegetation. Approx 65% nature, 35% weathered machine; overwhelmingly a high-end nature photograph of a real overgrown ruin, NOT a diagram or a sleek sci-fi rendering. The load-bearing limbs themselves are aged dark gunmetal/graphite, NOT wood with gadgets attached. Rough pitted plating, asymmetrical segmented sleeves, oxidized edges, patina and scratches show between thick cushions of vivid green moss, lush ivy, dangling vines, small ferns and epiphytes. A FEW varied-size riveted collars and round sensor hubs at irregular forks, mostly swallowed in moss, some cracked. Several long inlaid hairline pale-cyan (#bff0ff) glass/fiber channels still glow very faintly along main metal limbs, disappear beneath moss, then reappear. Keep several continuous readable stretches for later pulse animation. No neon or excessive glow. A few thin loose cables intertwine with hanging vegetation.
+
+COMPOSITION in final 2880x1800 coordinates: ONE HUGE connecting limb enters from OFFSCREEN RIGHT, edge centre y=500, its metal core 380–520 px thick at right edge. The limb extends left and spreads into a broad asymmetric, irregular canopy whose leftmost tips reach x=1250–1450. Botanical/structure silhouette occupies approximately the right 50–55% of width and y=245–1550, with gaps of sky. Tallest foliage y=245 or below. Main limbs fork at very different positions and angles, have dramatically different lengths and thicknesses; one bends up, another sags, some cross behind each other, one short broken stub. Dense growth in some areas and open gaps in others. NEVER evenly spaced branches, same-size nodes, mirrored forks, neat rows, or schematic repeated angles.
+Long Spanish moss and vines fall VERTICALLY downward at varied lengths, longest reaching y=1400–1580 on the right half. All foliage below y=700 must stay RIGHT of x=1270. No ground, trunk base, soil, other objects, floating isolated foliage, or roots reaching ground.
+Photorealistic botanical detail, translucent backlit lime green leaves and deep green shadow, bright natural daylight from upper RIGHT, cool sky fill on shaded metal, gentle rim highlights. Far tips slightly atmospheric, closest right-edge leaves can softly blur. Natural organic edges, no halos or white fringe.
+
+PRESERVE base sky gradient/clouds and all original navigation. ABSOLUTELY CLEAR: whole y<230 band, logo, Research / FAQs / Contact, meeting pill including the actual top-right position. Rectangle x=0–1250,y=700–1800 remains untouched pure sky. Entire left half mostly empty. No new text, labels, numbers, logos, watermarks, HUD, or UI. Render only one image, not a grid. Requested final size 2880 x 1800.
+
+VARIATION:
+01 BALANCED: Heavy moss cushions and draping ivy over a weathered metal limb. Three differently sized half-hidden hubs at uneven positions, faint cyan channels visible along several main limbs. A thick main bough twists down-left then a smaller bough rises back-left; a short fork behind, a broken stub. Natural disorder, plentiful hanging moss.
+
