+
+Add ONE abandoned futuristic machine sculpture shaped like an enormous irregular tree limb, reclaimed by decades of vegetation. Approx 65% nature, 35% weathered machine; overwhelmingly a high-end nature photograph of a real overgrown ruin, NOT a diagram or a sleek sci-fi rendering. The load-bearing limbs themselves are aged dark gunmetal/graphite, NOT wood with gadgets attached. Rough pitted plating, asymmetrical segmented sleeves, oxidized edges, patina and scratches show between thick cushions of vivid green moss, lush ivy, dangling vines, small ferns and epiphytes. A FEW varied-size riveted collars and round sensor hubs at irregular forks, mostly swallowed in moss, some cracked. Several long inlaid hairline pale-cyan (#bff0ff) glass/fiber channels still glow very faintly along main metal limbs, disappear beneath moss, then reappear. Keep several continuous readable stretches for later pulse animation. No neon or excessive glow. A few thin loose cables intertwine with hanging vegetation.
